course: dictionary
lesson: 10819
title: Vegetarian: a word about food and choice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vegetarian is a person who does not eat meat or fish. «Vegetarians eat no meat or fish, and vegans eat no food from animals at all.» The word tells you what a person chooses to leave out of their food.
explain: As an adjective, vegetarian describes food. A vegetarian meal has no meat or fish in it. Look at the words around it: «vegetarian option» on a school menu means there is a choice with no meat or fish.
explain: Some vegetarians still eat eggs and dairy, but vegans eat no animal foods at all. Read the whole sentence to see which kind of person is meant. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A vegetarian is a person who does not eat meat or fish.
fact: Vegetarian food has no meat or fish in it.
fact: Vegetarians may still eat eggs and dairy; vegans eat no food from animals at all.
fact: People may be vegetarian for health, belief, care for animals or the environment.
fact: In science, animals that eat only plants are called «herbivores», not «vegetarians».
exercise: «Vegetarians eat no meat or fish, and vegans eat no food from animals at all.» What does vegetarian mean? | A person who cooks meals at school | A person who grows vegetables for sale | *A person who does not eat meat or fish | A person who eats only meat
exercise: A school menu has a «vegetarian option». What does this tell you? | *There is a meal with no meat or fish in it | There is only meat on the menu | The food is free for everyone | The school has a new vegetable garden
exercise: In science, what do we call animals that eat only plants? | *Herbivores | Carnivores | Predators | Omnivores
test: Which people eat no food from animals at all? | Vegetarians who eat eggs | Herbivores | *Vegans | People who eat fish
test: «He is a gentle vegetarian munching about 18 kilograms of leaves a day.» What does the gorilla eat? | Meat | Fish | *Leaves | Eggs
exam: Priya says, «People are vegetarian for health, belief or love of animals, so never try to make them eat meat.» Why is this the right way to treat them? | *Because people choose what they eat for their own reasons | Because meat is dangerous to touch | Because school menus never change | Because vegetarians are always ill
